# Cloudflare Pages response headers. Vite copies public/ into dist/, so this
# file ships at the site root, which is where Pages reads it from.
#
# The first two are not optional and not a hardening measure: the WASM thread
# pool needs SharedArrayBuffer, browsers only expose SharedArrayBuffer to a
# cross-origin-isolated document, and a document is cross-origin isolated only
# with exactly this pair. Without them the startup capability check (F-UI-12)
# reports SharedArrayBuffer as FAIL and the app refuses to start.
#
# This is also why GitHub Pages cannot host this application — it serves no
# custom headers. See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, "Hosting".
#
# COEP require-corp additionally blocks any cross-origin subresource that does
# not send CORP. The app loads none — no CDN fonts, no third-party scripts, no
# external images — and that has to stay true.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
